{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289170-lunars-kickstarter-interview-with-eric-minton","id":1289170,"title":"Lunars Kickstarter Interview with Eric Minton","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-18T06:47:32-08:00","id":1289170,"title":"Lunars Kickstarter Interview with Eric Minton","content":"I had the pleasure of interviewing Eric Minton a couple weeks ago in preparation for the Lunar KS. We published the interview today and you can find it here: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com/bonus-episode-5-exalted-lunar-ks-interview-with-eric-minton\" target=\"_blank\">http://thestorytold.libsyn.com/bonus...th-eric-minton</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:10:26-08:00","id":1289201,"title":"","content":"Thanks for sharing this! It was a good interview! Great questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:28:32-08:00","id":1289206,"title":"","content":"Ah man... Americans pronounce Lunars very different to Brits. And Chimera. Which is unsurprising, but weird to hear.<br /> <br /> But it's a good interview.<br /> <br /> <br /> It was interesting to hear a little bit about the dominions. Looking forward to those!<br /> (That's the part of the fluff I'm most interested in. NPCs I wasn't that bothered by, but the locations in the Core I really like, so I'm excited about the Dominions.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-18-2019, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:52:49-08:00","id":1289216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289170-lunars-kickstarter-interview-with-eric-minton?p=1289206#post1289206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah man... Americans pronounce Lunars very different to Brits. And Chimera. Which is unsurprising, but weird to hear.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, not all Americans pronounce it as the interviewer did. I say it more like Luners, with less of an A emphasis. But I've met others who emphasize the A. Those people tend to do the same with Solars as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:55:39-08:00","id":1289218,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you guys liked it! We might be able to get Eric back on for another interview when we finally get around to our Dragon-Blooded book review. If the timing works out, I'll elicit questions from the forum here (thought the devs to a great job answering question here already!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:03:11-08:00","id":1289221,"title":"","content":"Nah, it's the &quot;r&quot;s. English and Welsh people lost the rhotic r a long time ago, most (but not all) Americans kept it (which... actually means it's more realistic to have American actors play medieval English people than English people. Which is weird), as did the Scots and Irish.<br /> We say /s\u0259\u028al\u0259/ and /lu:n\u0259/, that interviewer pronounced it /lu:n\u0251:r/.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:03:51-08:00","id":1289222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElfSpeaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289170-lunars-kickstarter-interview-with-eric-minton?p=1289218#post1289218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad you guys liked it! We might be able to get Eric back on for another interview when we finally get around to our Dragon-Blooded book review. If the timing works out, I'll elicit questions from the forum here (thought the devs to a great job answering question here already!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:23:34-08:00","id":1289226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289170-lunars-kickstarter-interview-with-eric-minton?p=1289221#post1289221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, it's the &quot;r&quot;s. English and Welsh people lost the rhotic r a long time ago, most (but not all) Americans kept it (which... actually means it's more realistic to have American actors play medieval English people than English people. Which is weird), as did the Scots and Irish.<br /> We say /s\u0259\u028al\u0259/ and /lu:n\u0259/, that interviewer pronounced it /lu:n\u0251:r/.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and your fancy edumacated words are too much for this Yank. (I'm afraid I'm not much of a linguist so I'm struggling to parse your descriptions of the difference. Definitely my failing though)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:27:34-08:00","id":1289227,"title":"","content":"It's fine, this is literally my job, I probably wouldn't understand the jargon of your job.<br /> <br /> We pronounce the suffixes <i>-er, -ar,</i> and <i>-or </i>as /\u0259/, which is the sound you make when you say <i>a</i> (as in the word <i>a</i>, like <i>a</i> man, <i>a</i> bee, <i>a</i> horse, etc, but not <i>a</i> like m<i>a</i>n or <i>pa</i>n or b<i>a</i>nd).<br /> Teach-a<br /> Doct-a<br /> Lawy-a<br /> Sol-a<br /> Lun-a<br /> <br /> Which means we pronounce Lunar almost identically to Luna.<br /> <br /> This is probably quite a tangent...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-18-2019, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:33:07-08:00","id":1289228,"title":"","content":"So, the dominions. I caught that there's one called the Empire of the Bear, which is quite imperialistic. Hmmm... sounds Northern to me, or maybe North-Eastern.<br /> <br /> Did anyone catch the others? I didn't quite catch them, as it was right near the end (don't have time to go back and listen again, I'm about to head off, I'll do it later if I have time).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:51:50-08:00","id":1289231,"title":"","content":"You and your Home Counties cultural imperalism again. In the West Country, we still use rhotic r. It's just northerners who don't speak proper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289170-lunars-kickstarter-interview-with-eric-minton?p=1289227#post1289227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fine, this is literally my job, I probably wouldn't understand the jargon of your job.<br /> <br /> We pronounce the suffixes <i>-er, -ar,</i> and <i>-or </i>as /\u0259/, which is the sound you make when you say <i>a</i> (as in the word <i>a</i>, like <i>a</i> man, <i>a</i> bee, <i>a</i> horse, etc, but not <i>a</i> like m<i>a</i>n or <i>pa</i>n or b<i>a</i>nd).<br /> Teach-a<br /> Doct-a<br /> Lawy-a<br /> Sol-a<br /> Lun-a<br /> <br /> Which means we pronounce Lunar almost identically to Luna.<br /> <br /> This is probably quite a tangent...</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5001-soul_porpoise","name":"soul_porpoise","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T11:26:43-08:00","id":1289243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289170-lunars-kickstarter-interview-with-eric-minton?p=1289227#post1289227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fine, this is literally my job, I probably wouldn't understand the jargon of your job.<br /> <br /> We pronounce the suffixes <i>-er, -ar,</i> and <i>-or </i>as /\u0259/, which is the sound you make when you say <i>a</i> (as in the word <i>a</i>, like <i>a</i> man, <i>a</i> bee, <i>a</i> horse, etc, but not <i>a</i> like m<i>a</i>n or <i>pa</i>n or b<i>a</i>nd).<br /> Teach-a<br /> Doct-a<br /> Lawy-a<br /> Sol-a<br /> Lun-a<br /> <br /> Which means we pronounce Lunar almost identically to Luna.<br /> <br /> This is probably quite a tangent...</div> </div> </div> </div>The easiest way i\u2019ve found to show the difference between Southern English and Urban Midwest (ie Hollywood generic) American accents is with \u201cwater\u201d.<br /> <br /> Southern English: Wata<br /> <br /> \u201cGeneric\u201d American: Wadder. (Americans don\u2019t think about it, but to other people\u2019s ears we really don\u2019t differentiate \u201ct\u201d and \u201cd\u201d sounds well at all)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-18-2019, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T12:29:14-08:00","id":1289267,"title":"","content":"Wata?<br /> What kind of posh toff pronounces the t?<br /> It's wa'a. As in &quot;Gimme a bo'ul of wa'a&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T12:38:54-08:00","id":1289269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289170-lunars-kickstarter-interview-with-eric-minton?p=1289267#post1289267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wata?<br /> What kind of posh toff pronounces the t?<br /> It's wa'a. As in &quot;Gimme a bo'ul of wa'a&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so happy with the direction this thread has gone, even if it's off-topic.<br /> <br /> But seriously, good Interview. Please interview these guys again in the future!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T13:12:16-08:00","id":1289280,"title":"","content":"Eric says &quot;It's a massive Charms chapter; we're still trying to figure out <b>what to cut</b>.&quot; (emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> So, I'm guessing the extra Charms we paid for in Strangers are already written, and otherwise we might not have gotten them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T14:25:54-08:00","id":1289311,"title":"","content":"More likely a mix.<br /> To be honest, more charms isn't always a good thing; it's worth considering if there are any charms the game is better off without, to improve overall quality.<br /> Probably it's not a problem, but worth the devs doing a last pass to check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T14:53:04-08:00","id":1289321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289170-lunars-kickstarter-interview-with-eric-minton?p=1289311#post1289311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More likely a mix.<br /> To be honest, more charms isn't always a good thing; it's worth considering if there are any charms the game is better off without, to improve overall quality.<br /> Probably it's not a problem, but worth the devs doing a last pass to check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.<br /> <br /> Like, maybe the Corebook should have been pruned of Demon-Wasting Rush, as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T05:31:45-08:00","id":1289478,"title":"","content":"I don't remember what that does, but I think you've got my point. I don't want to start an argument about particular charms, but there are 2 or 3 I think should just be cut straight out of the Core (as opposed to being rewritten).<br /> <br /> Charms that are so weak no-one takes them, or overpowered, or too similar to another charm, or which are written so vaguely that they'll cause arguments between players and ST, or thematically wrong, or which break the setting.<br /> <br /> I didn't see anything like that in the charms released so far, I think, so I'm not worried, I'm just making the point that there's other reasons to cut stuff beyond word count.<br /> <br /> Like how techniques got cut from MA.<br /> <br /> Or, you know, maybe it's wordcount.<br /> <br /> (I don't know for sure, but I heard writers only get paid for the wordcount of the book. If they write extra, they don't get paid for it. So it's fair to cut it, then release the cut stuff in another book, so they get paid.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-19-2019, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T07:23:19-08:00","id":1289516,"title":"","content":"So, Eric said that they got Shahan-ya from 1st ed Lunars.<br /> <br /> I don't remember that, does anyone else? Where was it, and what was the context?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T07:28:48-08:00","id":1289519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289170-lunars-kickstarter-interview-with-eric-minton?p=1289516#post1289516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Eric said that they got Shahan-ya from 1st ed Lunars.<br /> <br /> I don't remember that, does anyone else? Where was it, and what was the context?</div> </div> </div> </div>First Edition had a laundry list of &quot;social ranks&quot; that you climbed by acquiring Renown, which was a bullshit subsystem you don't need to know about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"dat